 "standard_url": "https://www.education.gov.za/Portals/0/CD/National%20Curriculum%20Statements%20and%20Vocational/CAPS%20SP%20%20MATHEMATICS%20GR%207-9.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Recognise and differentiate between monomials, binomials and trinomials; add and subtract like terms in algebraic expressions; multiply integers and monomials by monomials, binomials and trinomials; divide monomials, binomials and trinomials by integers or monomials; determine the product of two binomials; determine the squares, cubes, square roots and cube roots of single algebraic terms.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 8 algebraic expressions worksheets: like terms, multiplying and dividing terms, expanding brackets, binomials and common factors. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "Multiply every term in the bracket.",
 "key_sub": "Add only like terms.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Only like terms can be added: 3x² + 5x − x² = 2x² + 5x.</li><li>Multiply terms: multiply the numbers and add the exponents. 3a² × 4a = 12a³.</li><li>Expand: multiply every term in the bracket. −2(x − 5) = −2x + 10.</li><li>Two binomials: (x + 3)(x + 4) = x² + 4x + 3x + 12 = x² + 7x + 12.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>(2x − 1)(x + 5)</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>2x² + 10x − x − 5</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 2x² + 9x − 5</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Unlike terms</td><td>x² and x are not like terms.</td></tr><tr><td>The first term only</td><td>Multiply every term in the bracket.</td></tr><tr><td>Signs</td><td>−2 × −5 = +10.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does CAPS Grade 8 say about expressions?",
   "a": "Add, subtract, multiply and divide algebraic terms, expand products of a monomial and a binomial and of two binomials, and simplify expressions."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is a binomial?",
   "a": "An expression with two terms, like x + 3."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is 6x²y ÷ 2x?",
   "a": "3xy."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is factorising?",
   "a": "Writing an expression as a product, like 4x + 8 = 4(x + 2)."
  }
